      "problem": "Expressed as a fraction, $(-13)÷(-5)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have to divide a negative number $(-13)$ by another negative number $(-5).$ So the result will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-13)÷(-5)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $13$ by $5$ without any signs: $13÷5=\\frac{13}{5}.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n(-13)÷(-5)=\\frac{13}{5}.\n$$",
